# Expense Reimbursement Policy
**Daisy Health**
**Policy ID:** HR-EX-004
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** June 1, 2025
**Owner:** Finance and People Operations

---

## Purpose

Daisy Health reimburses employees for reasonable, work-related expenses incurred while performing their job duties. This policy explains what is covered, how to submit expenses, and what is not reimbursable.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all full-time and part-time Daisy Health employees. Contractors submit expenses per their individual agreements.

---

## 1. General Reimbursement Principles

Daisy Health will reimburse expenses that are:

- **Necessary** — required to do your job
- **Reasonable** — consistent with standard business practice and not excessive
- **Approved** — pre-approved by your manager when required
- **Documented** — supported by a receipt or invoice

Employees should spend Daisy Health funds as carefully as they would their own money. When in doubt about whether an expense is covered, ask your manager before spending.

---

## 2. Home Office Stipend

Full-time remote employees receive a **one-time home office stipend of $500** to set up their workspace. This is available upon hire and covers items such as:

- Monitor or monitor stand
- Keyboard and mouse
- Desk or ergonomic chair
- Webcam or headset
- Desk lamp or other workspace accessories

### How to Claim

Submit receipts through the Expense Portal within **60 days of your hire date**. Purchases must be made within your first 90 days of employment. The stipend does not roll over or carry over to future years.

Part-time employees are not eligible for the home office stipend.

---

## 3. Internet Reimbursement

Full-time remote employees may be reimbursed up to **$50/month** for home internet service. To claim:

- Submit a copy of your monthly internet bill through the Expense Portal
- Only the base internet service is reimbursable — not streaming bundles, cable TV, or phone service
- Reimbursement is processed monthly with payroll

---

## 4. Equipment

Daisy Health provides all employees with a company-issued laptop. If your role requires additional equipment beyond the standard laptop (e.g., a second monitor for clinical documentation), submit a request to IT through the IT Help Portal.

**Personal equipment purchases** (beyond the home office stipend) require **prior written approval** from your manager and Finance. Unapproved equipment purchases will not be reimbursed.

---

## 5. Professional Development and Continuing Education

Daisy Health supports employee growth through a **$1,000 annual professional development stipend**. This covers:

- Online courses and certifications
- Conference registration fees
- Professional memberships and dues
- Clinical continuing education (CE) credits for licensed staff
- Books or learning materials directly related to your role

### How to Claim

Submit receipts through the Expense Portal. Expenses over $500 require manager pre-approval before purchase. The stipend resets each January 1 and does not roll over.

---

## 6. Licensure and Credentialing Fees

Clinical staff may be reimbursed for the following:

- **State licensure renewal fees** — up to $300 per license per renewal cycle
- **DEA registration fees** — fully reimbursed for applicable clinical roles
- **Board certification fees** — up to $500 per certification exam, once per exam per year
- **Compact licensure fees** — reimbursed for compact licenses required for Daisy Health patient care

See the Licensure and Credentialing Policy (HR-LC-004) for full details on licensure support.

---

## 7. Travel Expenses

While Daisy Health is a virtual-first company, some employees may travel for company meetings, conferences, or offsites. Approved travel expenses include:

### Airfare

- Economy class is required for flights under 5 hours
- Business class requires VP-level pre-approval
- Book at least **14 days in advance** when possible to minimize cost
- Use the company's preferred booking tool when available

### Hotel

- Reimbursable up to **$200/night** in standard markets; up to **$350/night** in high-cost cities (San Francisco, New York, Boston)
- Incidentals charged to the room are the employee's responsibility unless pre-approved

### Ground Transportation

- Rideshare (Uber, Lyft) or taxi to/from airport: reimbursable
- Personal car mileage: reimbursed at the current **IRS standard mileage rate** (2025: $0.70/mile)
- Rental cars require manager pre-approval and must use Daisy Health's preferred rental vendor

### Meals During Travel

- Reimbursable up to **$75/day** (breakfast, lunch, dinner combined)
- Alcohol is not reimbursable
- Meals with clients or external partners may exceed the daily limit with prior approval and documentation of business purpose

---

## 8. Non-Reimbursable Expenses

The following are not reimbursable under any circumstances:

- Personal meals (non-travel)
- Alcohol
- Personal entertainment (movies, sports events, etc.)
- Gym memberships or fitness equipment
- Personal cell phone plans
- Traffic or parking tickets
- First-class or business-class travel without VP approval
- Expenses without receipts over $25
- Gifts for colleagues without prior HR approval
- Any expense not directly related to Daisy Health business

---

## 9. How to Submit Expenses

All expense reimbursements are submitted through the **Daisy Health Expense Portal** at expenses.daisyhealth.com.

- Attach original receipts for all expenses over $25
- Submit expenses within **30 days** of the purchase date — late submissions may be denied
- Include a brief business purpose note for each expense
- Manager approval is required before submission for expenses over $500
- Approved expenses are reimbursed via direct deposit within **2 pay cycles**

---

## 10. Policy Violations

Submitting fraudulent expense claims, misrepresenting business purposes, or intentionally circumventing this policy constitutes misconduct and may result in:

- Repayment of the disputed amount
- Formal disciplinary action
- Termination
- Referral to legal authorities in cases of fraud

